How the App Works

The deployed app is a Streamlit application (streamlit_app.py):

User selects Text (transcript) or Audio (recording) as input.
Text path: upload/paste a .cha transcript (participant speech marked *PAR:) → 11 features extracted → Logistic Regression pipeline → prediction + confidence (~76% expected accuracy).
Audio path: upload a recording → 88 eGeMAPS features extracted via openSMILE → SVM pipeline → prediction + confidence (~62% expected accuracy).
Each model's cross-validated accuracy is shown alongside its prediction so users can calibrate trust between the two paths.
A visible disclaimer reminds users this is a research/screening demo validated only on the Cookie Theft task.

A separate FastAPI service (transcript_files/app.py) also exposes the text model as an alternative API, independent of the Streamlit app.

