Key Design Decisions
Models are not merged/ensembled. The text (552 rows) and audio (395 rows) datasets have no dependable 1:1 join between recordings and transcripts, so a fused prediction would require guessing at the match-up. Each model scores independently.
Text model is the recommended path, given its clearly stronger accuracy (76.3% vs. 61.8%). The audio model is kept available for exploration/comparison, with accuracy shown transparently.
Streamlit and FastAPI kept separate. streamlit_app.py is the user-facing deliverable; transcript_files/app.py is an alternative/internal API for the text model only.
Speaker-grouped CV for audio avoids the same speaker appearing in both train and test folds, which would otherwise inflate reported accuracy.
